      "_id": "61686e5fbece1a4b59f25a05",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5f99a97e4d4afb3fb6674ca5",
        "alias": "Raisin Yak",
        "aliasID": "65c26da3ed6eefce4c4d1463",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/bb4656a7e1413dbb08dcad2351d7be2a.png",
        "created": "2020-10-28T17:25:18.378Z",
        "name": "M E R C",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "m-e-r-c"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5b0746088fa72313783e3269",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2021-10-14T17:52:31.729Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 9,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "61621b5faf145237ca045023",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 9
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The current implementation of the blocking system is flawed. This may be a good time to consider addressing this as the \"Here\" Menu would be a perfect use case for the proposed changes. \nIssue: When a user blocks you, you can't see them in social. Limited admin tools for Instance Owners can make this an issue. It can also make initiating a vote kick difficult to impossible. It can also create further abuse by allowing someone to spite block people in return for being blocked, target block instance owners and masters or target block world authors. Instance Owners are also not always around, leading to openings for abuse where the lobby doesn't have any realistic courses of action as they may be blocked by the malicious user.\nProposal: Emulate something similar to Discords blocking methodology. Blocking should not hide users from the \"Here\" menu. If you join an instance with someone who has you blocked, you should be able to tell by looking at the \"here\" menu. You shouldn't be able to interact with this person, a block should indeed mean a block, but you should be able to tell they're indeed in the lobby. This would remove spite blocking entirely as even if two people block each other, they can still see that they are in the lobby or not so makes it entirely moot. This also wouldn't negate the Instance Owner, world author, or world moderators from taking action as even if they get maliciously blocked, they can still see the person in \"Here\" and take action as needed. \nGist: Everyone should be able to see blocked users and users who have them blocked via the \"Here\" menu but not interact with them. This would fix the main crux of the problem.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
