      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5df86a5bfc2e6975420f5c28|full_name}: The system added to build 1145 is still not a complete solution to the problems people have posted about.  World and instance owners having exclusive access to the \"user who have you blocked\" is a bad thing.\nPeople in public worlds can't start votekicks against anyone who has them blocked (from my experience votekicks never even start properly).  If you are helping moderate a large instance, you can't properly inform the instance/world owner of the bad actor.  As other comments have noted, this is simply further driving people to use alternative tools like log parsers, the in-game players list debug menu, and malicious client modifications to provide basic information that by all means should exist.\nHiding the list of people who have you blocked only in the social menus serves no purpose.  They are still in the world.  They will produce notifications in Udon powered worlds with player join/leave notifications.  They will still be able to pick up objects and interact with the functions in a world.  Not only is the current system counterproductive, it is ineffective.  \nThis needs to be fixed before it becomes another half-thought-out half-assed \"feature\" that further drives people to download cheats for a game where you talk to people.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
